WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.080 --> 00:00:06.140
Robert: I work at a small lobbying firm downtown,
about two blocks from the White House. Basically

00:00:06.140 --> 00:00:11.349
what I do is I do a lot of research for the
senior staff and write up memos. It's very

00:00:11.349 --> 00:00:16.139
hands-on experience. While you may find yourself
occasionally making a cup of coffee, you're

00:00:16.139 --> 00:00:20.439
also probably going to committee hearings
up the hill or you're doing actual research

00:00:20.439 --> 00:00:24.779
that senior staff will then use to bring in
business. You really get to see the fruits

00:00:24.779 --> 00:00:30.449
of your labor in your internship in D.C.
You should do Hillsdale WHIP because it's

00:00:30.449 --> 00:00:35.949
such a great opportunity to get both great
work experience for your resume, but also

00:00:35.949 --> 00:00:41.760
great academic experience. As someone who
did the freshman courses of western heritage

00:00:41.760 --> 00:00:46.909
and great books, the great stuff that Hillsdale's
all about, to then come back out here to WHIP

00:00:46.909 --> 00:00:52.820
and take the statesmanship with Dr. Spalding
or history of the Cold War with Dr. Moreno,

00:00:52.820 --> 00:00:57.520
I really fell in love with Hillsdale College.
That's something that WHIP does for people.

